      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Looks like this is also running on the wrong thread.\n\nThanks for pointing this out done. Yeah, this is running on BR itself (which I guess runs on SystemServer thread or main UI thread?). \n\n\u003e For Q we can probably just run the broadcast receiver on the handler thread. \n\nMakes sense. Done. Note that I think all of ACTION_USER_* should be fine to run on CS handler, therefore I\u0027m going to pass in mHandler when registering mIntentReceiver (For ex - onUserStart also leads to calling updateCapabilities, although VPN shouldn\u0027t be running when a user is added, but I think it is probably better to be consistent). LMK if you think we should only migrate onUserAdded and onUserRemoved calls to CS handler (and not others).\n\n\u003e For P we need to consider the implications carefully.\n\nAck. For P, we will anyways need to cherry-pick changes carefully.\n\n\u003e Specifically, it looks like we\u0027d need to register the two BroadcastReceivers that listen for ACTION_USER_* so that they run on the ConnectivityService handler thread.\n\nAll the ACTION_USER_* are part of mIntentReceiver (on Q). I don\u0027t understand why we would need to register two BRs?",
      "parentUuid": "82f2842a_b21caff2",
